{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562307-v5-new-takes-on-compulsions","id":1562307,"title":"[V5] New Takes on Compulsions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-29T10:12:33-07:00","id":1562307,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [V5] New Takes on Compulsions","content":"The goal here is to post Compulsions and rules for them that change the themes of the game. They may be in addition to the existing ones or a substitute.<br /> <br /> I'll begin with a system to substitute the current one:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><b><u>Temptations of the Beast</u></b></span></span><br /> <br /> Current Compulsions are too strong behavioral drives focused on immediate action. They have a heavy penalty, demand immediate action, with little room to chose how to end them.<br /> <br /> This is interesting as exploration of the Beast as a curse that drives you to inevitable evil, but poor for an exploration of choices, of evil as an easy path rather than a coerced one.<br /> <br /> VtM was originally the later type of game. The narrator presenting degeneration as inevitable, contrasted with rules that make resistance an actually feasible choice if you put the effort, is the centerpiece of vampiric hypocrisy: there is no inevitability, it's a lie they tell themselves to hide from their own choices.<br /> <br /> In <i>Temptations of the Beast</i>, each Compulsion grows from a type of Frenzy. They're presented with 6 clear sections described below. They're not tame behaviors, but give you more options to resolve your situation. The sections are<br /> <br /> <i><b>Goal,</b></i> defined by the Beast's most immediate desire/need. Actions that detract or stall the goal are penalized by -1.<br /> - The key here is &quot;detract/stall&quot;. An action not geared towards the goal, but that don't make it less likely either, are not penalized. Even when a penalty applies, it's a more endurable one.<br /> <br /> A <i><b>Tell,</b></i> that makes the Beast beneath visible to everyone through attitude, from staring people as if they're plates of food to constant shifting to stay close to the exits, few people would need any roll to know exactly what the vampire feels, if not why. Usually the Tell has no effect on rolls and can be suppressed at will.<br /> <br /> But <b><i>Telltale Actions</i></b> change everything. It's a small list of actions related to the Tell. Once in each scene the Kindred must engage at least one such actions, meaning dedicate at least a few turns (or one when more is too disrupting) to that action alone, without dividing attention. If they're don't, next scene their Goal penalty increase to -2 and they can't hide the Tell.<br /> <br /> Finally, each has three <i>Resolution Clauses</i> to end the compulsion: <i><b>Indulging</b></i>, <i><b>Daysleep</b></i> and <i><b>Frenzy</b></i>. Any one of them is enough to conclude the Compulsion.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Indulging</b></i> is the most direct way to satisfy the Beast. It can be accomplished in short notice if the character want, but may harm people in the process. This is about what the Compulsions in the Core Book require, maybe a little more harsher to compensate the other two.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Daysleep</b></i> is the reward of patience. It requires giving the Beast its due without extremes and then sleeping it off.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Frenzy</b></i> is complete submission, though it may happen in a controlled manner. If the Kindred enters the specified Frenzy type for any reason, the Compulsion resolves. The vampire can, at any moment, chose to let the Compulsion flare into a full blown Frenzy, but cannot roll control of Ride the Wave when doing so.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Gluttonous Beast Compulsion</b></u><br /> <br /> <i><b>Goal</b></i>: the Beast lusts for blood beyond its needs. Actions that stall the next feeding are under a -1 penalty<br /> <br /> <i><b>Tell</b></i>: staring at blood vessels in preferred biting spots, sniffing for the smell of blood, entranced by red liquids. Hunger is evident, and everyone is a possible feast.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Telltales</b></i>: search a suitable victim; lick what looks like blood; bare fangs near warm skin.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Indulging</b></i>: Slake 5 Hunger in one scene<br /> <br /> <i><b>Daysleep</b></i>: at Hunger 1 or below<br /> <br /> <i><b>Frenzy</b></i>: Hunger<br /> <br /> <u><b>Wrathful Beast Compulsion</b></u><br /> <br /> <i><b>Goal</b></i>: impatience builds up, demanding direct and preferably physical solutions. Actions that avoid direct confrontation are at a -1 penalty.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Tell</b></i>: clenched teeth/fists, contorted face, growling, defiant glares, all worsening at minor or indirect issues. Visible tension as everything feels like an insult.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Telltales</b></i>: overtly take issue at something, punch or offend someone, break things.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Indulging</b></i>: exchange (deal + suffer) 2\u00d7 Stamina in Aggravated Health damage, or 5\u00d7 Stamina in Superficial Health damage, with living/undead, not objects.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Daysleep</b></i>: at Health or Willpower \u2264 1<br /> <br /> <i><b>Frenzy</b></i>: Fury<br /> <br /> <u><b>Panicked Beast Compulsion</b></u><br /> <br /> <i><b>Goal</b></i>: remove oneself from risk and remove risk from nearby. Actions that increase exposure to potential threats or unassessed contexts are at -1 penalty.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Tell</b></i>: eyes darting around looking for escape routes, tensed body ready to fight or flight, constant body reposition to optimize safety and distance. Obvious fear, they're all danger.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Telltales</b></i>: assessment of the area, removal of potential dangers, leave for a safer place.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Indulging</b></i>: assume complete control of your immediate environment, including witness, for a scene.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Daysleep</b></i>: alone, total darkness, no risk of fire.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Frenzy</b></i>: Terror/R\u00f6tschreck","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T11:09:28-07:00","id":1562309,"title":"","content":"How long have you been working on this list of descriptive compulsions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T11:33:56-07:00","id":1562312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1562307-v5-new-takes-on-compulsions?p=1562309#post1562309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long have you been working on this list of descriptive compulsions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some hours, took more time to write in the cellphone than to think of them.<br /> <br /> My problems with the official list is old, so I already knew what I liked, what I didn't, and why.<br /> <br /> Also, I wholeheartedly recommend getting rid of Clan Compulsions. They harm the game more than they contribute. They don't even help to play close to stereotype, because they're more likely to get in your way at doing so with a stupid sudden urge to mess with everything than they contribute to the long plan thinking that really forms clan culture.<br /> <br /> I'm currently playing as a Tzimisce. By myself I jote down a lot of notes about how my char is feeling about her new city and improvement plans that unconsciously play on her growing tendency to see this place as fundamentally hers.<br /> <br /> Big things. A new religion, a guardian deity for the city, organizing labor unions, influencing schools and shelters, altering local cuisine. It's not terrible stuff yet, although she's also trying to find a way to spike pastries with Blood and infect her games (she's a dev) with dataminers and backdoors, and even make local Vampires dependent on her software suites.<br /> <br /> Covetous, the Clan Compulsion, kicked out during my attempt to get close to a group of children that includes a Psychic I wanted to get ingratiate myself with for later ally or Ghoul. At the moment I was preparing to enter the house, so there was no NPCs around. Thanks to the Compulsion I, the Tzimisce...<br /> <br /> Stole two flags from their poles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}